  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two discs of same mass and different radii are made of different materials such that their thicknesses are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively. The densities of materials are in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. The moment of inertia of these discs respectively about their diameters will be in the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Mass of the disc in terms of density can be written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now moment of inertia of the disc about the diameter is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Required ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#961;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>&#961;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
